  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Lockheed Martin obligated $12.6B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date, across 234 awards with an average award size of $54M. Obligations are up 21.2% year over year. Obligations have climbed since FY21, moving from $4.7B in FY21 to $12.6B in FY26, with interim totals of $7.1B in FY22, $8.7B in FY23, $7.3B in FY24, and $10.4B in FY25. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the dominant market for Lockheed Martin in FY2026 to date at $11.4B. Other notable markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $824M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $91.7M. Contract activity is concentrated in aerospace and defense systems, with smaller pockets of work in logistics consulting, R&D in physical and engineering sciences, and engineering services. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations rather than full-year awards or total contract values.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Lockheed Martin's federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "Lockheed Martin obligated $12.6B in FY2026 to date, up 21.2% year over year. Obligations rose from $4.7B in FY21 to $12.6B in FY26, with intermediate totals of $7.1B in FY22, $8.7B in FY23, $7.3B in FY24, and $10.4B in FY25. The year-to-date figure is partial and reflects fiscal year to date obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where do Lockheed Martin's obligations concentrate by market?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounts for $11.4B of obligations in FY2026 to date. Other markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $824M, All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $91.7M, and Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services at $84.5M."
      }
